VU1 x86-64 JIT at the speed of the build's generated code, plus native-backend fixes it exposed.
JIT: every hot statement inline (flags, CLIP, ITOF/FTOI/ABS, Q unit, branches, flag-ring pushes), nrm() cache per block,
dead MAC stores removed, AVX three-operand encoding (GOW_VU1X_AVX=0: SSE4.1), entry-lane speculation with recompile on a
failed check (GOW_VU1X_SPECULATE=0 off), one reserved code range so JIT blocks chain past the prologue, GOW_VU1X_DUMP.
Fixes: re-registering a key keeps its timing table (use after free); chain() checks entry lanes itself; upper/lower
writes to the same VF register keep the upper result like the exact engine (vu1n_gen.py too); MAXi/MINIi results are not
assumed clean; recordMissHead does not append heads earlier sessions wrote. Tests: tests/vu1_bench.cpp, GOW_FUZZ_SPECIAL.

